# ── Pipeline output — regenerated every run (23-Sep-2026) ────────────────────
# A normal trading day left 72 tracked files modified: scan CSVs, board caches,
# status JSON, auto-pilot logs. That noise hides real changes and made "what did
# I actually edit today" a manual filter on every commit.
#
# Everything below is written BY the pipeline and reproducible by running it, so
# a fresh clone regenerates them on the first auto-pilot pass. Inputs are NOT
# here and stay tracked: My Portfolio.csv, MASTER_Golden_Picks.csv, sectors.db's
# mappings, and every .py/.pine.
#
# Same caveat as the block above: .gitignore does not untrack what is already
# tracked, and the contents stay in git HISTORY. The accompanying commit ran
# `git rm --cached` over the 87 files these patterns match.

# Screener and matcher output
FINAL_*.csv
FINAL_*.txt
SCREENER_*.csv
MASTER_scan_results.csv
Bull_Screener_Results.csv
Recovery_Screener_Results.csv
Stage2_*.csv
Strong_Leaders*.csv
Early_Birds*.csv
Recovery_Climax_Bounce*.csv
Recovery_Early_Birds*.csv
Recovery_RS_Survivors*.csv
Exit_Signals.csv
pullback_candidates.csv
ETF_*.csv
ETF_*.json
Screener CSVs/

